  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9dd3abbfc4a14c86845fd3430ee6c5da",
      "statement": "Screening is a deterministic gate that decides whether to spend the LLM budget on a document at all, routing both manifestly degraded and manifestly clean documents to a light path while reserving full judgment for genuinely ambiguous cases.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6364d8fa7ad5367013fce24946b1e93d33f86f05e0972610e19f4e5aee2c18e1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L21-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23579cef7e2b721ae7973dfb15549bd13653518de0b4f556d52b5bb07a03a584:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_screen.py#L16-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f97d69ff582d086b8bad09d1a70279c29a93244720a89ab802ba36828268114:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d9c3f423ffc47ef9377bafa4dc4baf0",
      "statement": "The screen's four outcomes carry verbatim French reason strings — gros_document_extraction_saine, extraction_degradee, signaux_propres and cas_limite — and the degradation and large-document reasons interpolate the measured signal values so the report shows the numbers behind the decision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/cli.py#L130-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ea56563e8627cff74f33be2c08b43c4aad2a83a842a55056898caf518201023:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L44-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36cffab506836871a1b236680478a74a831916d8fa3e7f4d94b80287f600cb88:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b4758ff762b64e79bdd943be4d0ac7da",
      "statement": "The large-document guardrail is evaluated first and requires several concordant healthy signals — token count above the large threshold together with acceptable parse confidence, bounded non-alpha fraction and healthy window-normalized TTR — routing such a document to full judgment because a low global TTR at that length is a length artifact rather than evidence of degradation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L16-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23a88f370074df7caedec7f97632702038ad5ba472d2490801d953ca5dc351e5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_screen.py#L47-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:367196538166943b6573dfc8f3eca9689040d3b3de039849748f1a956a605f62:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5ea4b2e18df471e9f561c84bb24dad2",
      "statement": "The large-document guardrail short-circuits the clean-signals shortcut as well as the degradation rule, so a large document is never skipped for being too clean either — it always receives a complete judgment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L38-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e91d879fa0058907fc54de5d0c10d354fc92b071466d5f45a5ec74201403f876:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L60-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d49a16ce0d9d0ee2e15772ab184ee5076960514f3cf6b88f04dc283a23d7a23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_884da4dd34d9486985adec5441b7d5e2",
      "statement": "A genuinely degraded large document still routes light because its window-normalized TTR fails the guardrail's condition and falls through to the degradation rule, a behaviour pinned by a test paired with the healthy-large-document case.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L44-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8efabb1bb3fb8a09fd5050a9a8b124c925f9adc3a1f2846d59b5efcc5b874d7c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_screen.py#L60-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67b83ca5d06c405065ea87f970e5e03bc63159004d4ff1e33e87a8ea38f93a48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33ea6d23d96b4d0395c3fbac7799971a",
      "statement": "The degradation rule triggers on any one of three independent signals — parse confidence below 0.5, non-alpha fraction above 0.40, or window-normalized TTR below 0.05 — so a single sufficient indication of a broken extraction is enough to divert the document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L50-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f58204477b7e506114e07fa7fd0838f322a1f2fbe818d5a71e60021b9b8df1d9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_screen.py#L16-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3eb37599abf43cb3c1aef1ece5c1c0c4d79cd3a82dce305f6556ce1b9de6764:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d5cfbb3d8de41e18f31b7e69bf23a0a",
      "statement": "Every screening rule uses the window-normalized MATTR rather than the global type-token ratio, with the global ratio read only as a fallback default when MATTR is absent, specifically to avoid confusing a long document with one having near-zero vocabulary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L24-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ce827fd3f2a4ce51b5d926e3829589591f3b98119e397798289ec49eccabbb9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/screen.py#L50-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f58204477b7e506114e07fa7fd0838f322a1f2fbe818d5a71e60021b9b8df1d9:"
